<title>JAPAN: TOKYO BOURSE IMPOSES 100 MLN YEN FINE ON NOMURA.</title>
<headline>TOKYO BOURSE IMPOSES 100 MLN YEN FINE ON NOMURA.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tokyo Stock Exchange (TSE) said on Friday that it has imposed a 100 million yen fine on scandal-hit Nomura Securities Co Ltd.  </p>
<p>The TSE said in a statement that it imposed the penalties because Nomura violated the securities law and the Commercial Code.</p>
<p>On Wednesday, a Nomura had to suspend part of its operations under administrative penalties for making illegal payoffs to a &quot;sokaiya&quot; corporate racketeer. Dai-Ichi Kangyo Bank Ltd (DKB) was also ordered to suspend some of its operations for its involvement in the scandal.</p>
</text>
